In article <C2u9rA.FK9@news.cso.uiuc.edu> CHU@UIMRL3.MRL.UIUC.EDU
(Kelvin Chu, UIUC Physics) writes:
>Hi fellow NetHack addicts;

>1.  I (perhaps stupidly) managed to eat a nymph corpse and now and teleporting
>	involuntarily all over the bloody dungeon.  How do I stop this?  (or 
>	must I get a ring of teleport control?)  

You can't stop it really.  It's theoretically possible, but not really
practical or desirable.  You could get a gremlin to steal it from you,
but chances are good he would steal a lot of other, more useful
intrinsics first - or he'd probably kill you.  Anyway, you have to
have teleport in order to get teleport control, and you need teleport
control to get to the bottom of the dungeon.  If you get a wish, wish
for 3 blessed tins of tengu meat.  This will give you teleport control
(probably) without needing to wear a ring.

>2.  Do tinned foods just not (um...) hack it; are they particularly low in 
>	nutritional value?  I found after clearing out a throne room that when
>	I tinned everything, I just spent time eating _all_ the tins
>	immediately afterwards (this was before I was the King o' teleport)
>	because they didn't fill me up.  Do I have some weird intrinsic, or
>	is this just the case for unblessed tins?  

As was mentioned before, the only tins with any food value to speak of
are tins of spinach, which you can't create with a kit.  I would
recommend only tinning monsters that could give you worthwhile
intrinsics, perhaps even ones you already have, in case you get
attacked by a gremlin.  Btw, a blessed tinning kit makes blessed tins.

